-- title:
--   Lemma 14, p.10 — $\mathcal K\supseteq\mathcal G^\circ$
-- statement:
--   Let $\delta$ be a control on a finite set $S$, $t$ a word with $|\delta(S,t)|$ minimal, $S_{ret}=\delta(S,t)$, and let $M_a$ be invertible rational $d\times d$ letter matrices with $\mathcal G$ the Zariski closure of the group they generate. Let $\mathcal K$ be the Zariski closure of $\{M_z:z\in L_{S_{ret}}\}$, where $L_{S_{ret}}$ is the monoid of words fixing every state of $S_{ret}$. Then
--   $$\mathcal K\supseteq\mathcal G^\circ.$$
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: a CCRA computing an invertible $f$ with minimal representation $(\lambda,(M_a),\gamma)$ of dimension $d\ge1$ → any finite control $(S,\delta)$ and any invertible rational letter matrices $M_a$, $d\ge0$; reason: the lemma and its proof use only the control and the invertibility of the $M_a$; the paper's setting is a special case
--   - encoding: Zariski closure via polynomials in the entries and $\det^{-1}$ → polynomials in the entries, closed sets taken relative to $GL_d(\overline{\mathbb Q})$; reason: multiplying by a power of $\det$, a unit on $GL$, gives the same closed subsets of $GL$
--   - encoding: identity component $\mathcal G^\circ$ of the algebraic group → the union of all Zariski-connected subsets of $\mathcal G$ containing $1$ (the connected component of $1$); reason: this is the identity component of a linear algebraic group; its group and finite-index properties (A1) are theorems, not definitions
-- source:
--   Zeng–Cao–Dai–Wang–Ding, Copyless Cost Register Automata and Algebraic Groups, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 434d3094df2665371c402d5b5291b3c7f3a27a0d79384e4a8ec3ca3a46a92543), Lemma 14, p.10 (PDF p.12)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CopylessCRA_CCRA
import Definitions.Def_CopylessCRA_zariskiClosure
import Definitions.Def_CopylessCRA_returnWords

namespace CopylessCRA

/-- **Lemma 14.** `𝒦 ⊇ 𝒢°`, where `𝒢` is the Zariski closure of the group generated by the letter
matrices and `𝒦` is the Zariski closure of `{M_z : z ∈ L_{S_ret}}`.

Zeng–Cao–Dai–Wang–Ding, *Copyless Cost Register Automata and Algebraic Groups*, STOC 2027
submission (manuscript sha256 434d3094…), Lemma 14, p.10 (PDF p.12).

**Formalization Note** The §4 setting fixes a CCRA computing an invertible `f` with minimal
representation `(λ, (M_a), γ)`; the lemma and its proof use only the control `(S, δ)`, the word `t`
with `|δ(S, t)|` minimal, and invertible letter matrices `M_a`, so it is stated in that generality
(a generalization: no registers, no minimality, `d ≥ 1` not assumed). -/
theorem lemma_14 {S α : Type*} [Fintype S] [DecidableEq S] [Fintype α] (δ : S → α → S)
    {d : ℕ} (M : α → Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ) (hM : ∀ a, IsUnit (M a)) (t : List α)
    (ht : IsMinImageWord δ t) :
    identityComponent (zariskiGroup M) ⊆ returnClosure M (returnWords δ (imageWord δ t)) := by sorry

end CopylessCRA
